=== REASONING ===
Persistence orchestration belongs in AutomationRepo: handlers normalize typed input and pass AutomationStepWrite DTOs; repository methods own SQL transaction boundaries.
CreateWithSteps and UpdateWithSteps use DB.WithTx; parent row, automation_steps inserts/deletes, and CTI child writes flow through the same tx executor.
UpdateWithSteps locks the parent automation row with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE, deletes replacement steps inside the same transaction, and relies on FK cascade for child rows.
Handler side effects (audit and MQTT reload) occur only after repository create/update returns successfully, so they run after commit.
=== CHANGES ===
No additional code edits were required after survey: allowed files already contain the transactional typed-step persistence and rollback coverage required by this phase.
